  "question": {
    "text": "Two charges of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi></math> are situated at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> respectively. The electric flux through a sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math> having centre at origin is:",
