  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/48011775-356e-42e9-9120-9c61dfa20058.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 222px;\"/></p><p>As can be seen from the figure above, only the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>Q</mi></math> charge is inside the spherical region.</p><p>The formula to calculate the flux through the surface is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>enc</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, the flux through the given surface can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p>",
